Subject: [PATCH] Complete explicit policy activation on its eligible radio

Select an idle, executable radio rather than the arbitrary AL vector front.
An explicit SetPolicy has one candidate, so that owner sends the device-wide
policy even when a sibling is still onboarding. Misconfigured is a stable
post-timeout state from which an idempotent policy can restore reporting.
Keep automatic onboarding's existing multi-radio policy coordination.

The CLI must inspect the native status: a non-null response can reject a
command as busy. Retry only that explicit non-admission within the existing
eight-second policy budget; never treat a missing or rejected result as
successful activation. No metric values or convergence gates are changed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

